---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'
import Layout from '~/layouts/Layout.astro'

import '~/styles/projects.scss'

import itab from '~/assets/projects/discord/itab.png'
import types from '~/assets/projects/discord/types.png'
import ops from '~/assets/projects/discord/ops.png'
import rq from '~/assets/projects/discord/rq.png'
import roul from '~/assets/projects/discord/roul.png'
---

<Layout title={['Projects', 'Discord Bot']}>
  <div class='exp'>
    <div>
      This is my very own Discord bot, completely made from scratch.
      <Image src={itab} alt={'itab'} width={360} loading={'eager'} />
    </div>
    <div>
      If I'm being honest, the code is <b>extremely</b> messy and definitely needs a rewrite.
      There's so many folders and functions and files to manage and remember where things are and it's just all over the place.
    </div>
    <div>
      Initially, this bot was just meant to send the messages for my JetSpotter script and help view statistics,
      like most common plane types or most common operators.
      <Image src={types} alt={'types'} width={480} />
      <Image src={ops} alt={'ops'} width={480} />
    </div>
    <div>
      But now there's a whole bunch of other features! Some commands are just mirrors of cool Twitch bot commands I've seen before.
      A couple examples are <code>/rq</code> and <code>/roulette</code>.
      <Image src={rq} alt={'rq'} width={720} />
      <Image src={roul} alt={'roul'} width={480} />
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>